# ui_big_fig.steps with 基本図形編集 running as a process (design 11.3), for tools/ui_run.py:
# a figure of 10000 rectangles and two lines of 2000 points (mkbig fig 10000 2000) opened with
# pfig, all picked, cut to the tray, moved back, closed (saved), the record's sum kept, opened
# again and closed: the record is the same. The process says how many shapes there are and how
# many are picked after each command ("figure: shapes N picked M"), what the desktop's figure
# editor answers to the step shapes; the times are the host's, from the key to that line.
# Keys with Ctrl (01): A 04, X 1B, Z 1D, E 08.
mkbig fig 10000 2000
logmark
hostmark
pfig big
expectsincein 60 figure: opened 画用紙 shapes 10002
hosttime open 30000
shot big_fig_proc_open
logmark
hostmark
key 04 01
expectsincein 60 figure: shapes 10002 picked 10002
hosttime pickall 10000
logmark
hostmark
key 1B 01
expectsincein 60 figure: shapes 0 picked 0
hosttime cut 30000
logmark
hostmark
key 1D 01
expectsincein 90 figure: shapes 10002 picked 10002
hosttime moveback 60000
shot big_fig_proc_back
logmark
hostmark
key 08 01
expectsincein 60 figure: closed
hosttime closed 30000
sum
keep saved
logmark
hostmark
pfig big
expectsincein 60 figure: opened 画用紙 shapes 10002
hosttime reopen 30000
logmark
key 08 01
expectsincein 60 figure: closed
sum
same saved
absent !OACV!
